  "live_records": {
    "q-162924": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162924",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14129388/assets/ff6c3e308d89c9d07cff993f097fe2fcfafb22dab3399b9056f8db167b1b4b80.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curves $y=2x$ and $y={x}^{2}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. If the mass density function of $D$ is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=6x+14y,$ find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14129388/assets/fb20e4c3052e28aeb2e6dad5054b0458db2d3b23d10991cfae27b5b00655a8fe.png)\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2x}{x}^{2}(6x+14y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2x}6{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[6{x}^{3}y+7{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(12{x}^{4}+28{x}^{4})-(6{x}^{5}+7{x}^{6})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}40{x}^{4}-6{x}^{5}-7{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[8{x}^{5}-{x}^{6}-{x}^{7}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =256-64-128 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
