    "q-163145": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163145",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\cdot x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}x{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{6}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}-0 \\\\  & =1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis is $1.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
