    "q-163147": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163147",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,e\\le x\\le {e}^{3},\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{e}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis is $7.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
