    "q-163177": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163177",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis.\nFind the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k[x]_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =k(2-0)(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{3M}{2}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[x]_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}(2-0)(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
